{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791431153,"nonce":"Te7PZnKpJ/LEyixv1uZim6M3afM=","title":"Context.typeof loses the ValueType result of Type.typeof","message":"The native-valid /tmp/TypeofTyping.hx defines a macro that returns haxe.macro.TypeTools.toString(Context.typeof(e)), then prints name(Type.typeof(12)). Native Haxe prints ValueType. Rayzor prints Dynamic. Logs: /tmp/rayzor-typeof-typing-native-v1.log and /tmp/rayzor-typeof-typing-before-v1.log.\n\nThe backend reflection identity issue is tracked under c4b7f062533d305ec1b59fb702987e7043584a73aabd7b031be2705b54df763c. A backend recovery for the runtime ValueType representation does not by itself correct the macro-visible frontend type. ensure_known_static_method_type in ast_lowering/expr/calls.rs attempts to resolve ValueType by its short name and falls back to Dynamic; enum declarations and imported method symbols need examination before narrowing the root cause.","files":null}]}